      "order": 5,
      "bbox": [
        303,
        226,
        339,
        915
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἔξεστι ‘it is permitted, it is possible’ works in the same way, except that it takes a dat. (not acc.) of the person, e.g.",
      "lang": "en",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 6,
      "bbox": [
        351,
        246,
        388,
        893
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "ἔξεστι τῷ ἀνθρώπῳ ἐξελθεῖν ‘it is permitted/possible for the man to go out’, i.e. ‘the man is permitted/allowed to go out’, ‘the man may go out’",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "order": 7,
      "bbox": [
        399,
        246,
        419,
        908
      ],
      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(Cf. ἀνάγκη ἐστί which can take either acc. or dat. and infinitive: 153[b].)",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": null,
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
      "uncertain": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
